// EXPECT: [E100]
// ★ `effects write` IS AN ASSERTION OF NOTHING, so it is not sayable.
//
// The effect means "writes mutable GLOBAL state", and Lain has none: a top-level `var` is [E100],
// so the bound's domain is EMPTY by language design. Declaring it was therefore always satisfied,
// and nothing rejects a claim for being merely true — which is why it survived the audit that
// named it by three months. A vacuous bound passes every check there is.
//
// The diagnostic names the two real things a programmer might have meant: mutation through a `var`
// PARAMETER, which is in the signature rather than the row (and whose write footprint is tracked
// by a separate, live mechanism), or `effects io`.
func f(var x i32) effects write {
    x = 1
}
func main() i32 { return 0 }
